WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.520
A temperature anomaly compares an observation with a chosen

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.520
average.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.920
A negative value is cooler than the reference.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.860
A series can have brief dips and rises while its longer trend

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.220
still goes up.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.160
A tree adds a layer as it grows.

00:00:16.605 --> 00:00:20.945
Ring width can respond to moisture as well as temperature.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:25.555
Cave deposits, ice, and fossils record other conditions.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.670
Compare independent evidence before assigning a climate cause

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.190
to any one proxy.
